@format 1
@id media-loading.common.docket-insertion
@title Docket insertion
@section Media loading
@area Common
@entry docket-request
@summary Trace already-resolved media paths through LDocketPathsAdd, Files rebuilding, first-new-item selection, and the later PListItemsAdd notification.
@related media-loading.common.files-intake, media-loading.in-edit, media-loading.in-audio, media-loading.in-merge, media-loading.in-worklist, media-loading.in-staged-workspace
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag docket

@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList

[docket-request] Resolved media paths submitted to docket <input>
~ This starts with resolved media paths submitted to program file list.
[Technical explanation]
= A caller already has media paths and calls LDocketPathsAdd, optionally supplying an existing batch and delivered flag.
> docket-add

[docket-add] Docket add result <decision>
~ The program checks whether any new media entries were added to the program file list.
[Technical explanation]
- Ignore paths already listed, create a batch only when none was supplied, append new entries, and only for new entries raise LDocketChange followed by LDocketAdded @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
? "At least one new entry" > docket-change
? "Nothing new" > no-new-entry

[docket-change] Files rows and lock state refresh <process>
~ This step handles files rows and lock state refresh.
[Technical explanation]
- Raise LDocketChange first; the Files subscriber rebuilds rows, reapplies selection visuals, and publishes current lock state before LDocketAdded is invoked @ docket.LDocketRaise(...)
  @ list.PListDocketHandle(...)
> added-notification

[added-notification] First-new-item selection <process>
~ This step handles first-new-item selection.
[Technical explanation]
- Handle LDocketAdded by selecting the first newly added entry; PListSelectApply synchronously reaches PListCurrentApply and publishes PListPathChange before this handler resumes @ list.PListDocketAddHandle(...)
  @ list.PListSelectApply(...)
  @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> items-added

[items-added] Added-items notification <process>
~ This step handles added-items notification.
[Technical explanation]
- After the synchronous PListPathChange invocation returns, invoke PListItemsAdd for the complete set of newly added entries @ list.PListDocketAddHandle(...)
> notifications-complete

[notifications-complete] Docket insertion notifications complete <output>
~ The new media entries are now represented in the program file list and announced to the tab.
[Technical explanation]
= The first new path has been published through PListPathChange, then PListItemsAdd has announced the complete addition set. Downstream PListPathChange subscribers are outside this map; Audio, Edit, and Merge loading maps cover their PListItemsAdd initialization.

[no-new-entry] No new docket entry <output>
~ No new media entry was added to the program file list.
[Technical explanation]
= LDocketChange, LDocketAdded, PListPathChange, and PListItemsAdd are not raised for paths that were all already listed.
